{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018M99KZ2rSGBC2D7vRJRSVT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"}]\n\nI found information about CoRL 2026. While I found some general CoRL information and author instructions, the search results don't contain a specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines document or review form yet. \n\nHowever, here's what I found:\n\n**CoRL 2026 Author Information:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n**From Previous CoRL Conferences:**\nThe search results included reviewer guidelines from CoRL 2023 and 2024. For example, CoRL reviewers are asked to evaluate papers based on relevance (whether the paper addresses a robot learning problem and applies or improves a learning-based method), whether the method is evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both, and whether the CoRL audience will be interested in reading the paper.\n\nFor the most up-to-date CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the official CoRL 2026 website at corl.org or the OpenReview page for CoRL 2026, as these guidelines may be released closer to the review period.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f290d644-682c-40ce-bbe2-cd72e060667b","uuid":"1a590dc9-8ab5-4463-9a0b-a9eb4439fc47","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:44:13.646Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01GspBf1dYsCyLKpGdQ6zNbU","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CVPR 2026 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://cvpr.thecvf.com/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelinesq"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"}]},"I found information about CoRL 2026. While I found some general CoRL information and author instructions, the search results don't contain a specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines document or review form yet. \n\nHowever, here's what I found:\n\n**CoRL 2026 Author Information:**\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\n**From Previous CoRL Conferences:**\nThe search results included reviewer guidelines from CoRL 2023 and 2024. For example, CoRL reviewers are asked to evaluate papers based on relevance (whether the paper addresses a robot learning problem and applies or improves a learning-based method), whether the method is evaluated in simulation, on real robots, or both, and whether the CoRL audience will be interested in reading the paper.\n\nFor the most up-to-date CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the official CoRL 2026 website at corl.org or the OpenReview page for CoRL 2026, as these guidelines may be released closer to the review period."],"durationSeconds":6.387280394000001}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ybm7kJpEUwVTDDx3T9uVkw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 2024 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric acceptance rate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"About Our Ratings & Reviews [2025]\",\"url\":\"https://educationdata.org/about-our-ratings-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CORL 2024 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2024-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Po-Jen/Robotics-Conference-Acceptance-Rate: Statistics of acceptance rate for the main robotics conference · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Po-Jen/Robotics-Conference-Acceptance-Rate\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information about CoRL reviewer guidelines and instructions, though the specific details vary by year:\n\n## CoRL 2024 Reviewer Guidelines\n\nSubmissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\nThe review process involves Associate Chairs (ACs) identifying desk rejection candidates using specified criteria, with the Program Committee (PC) making final decisions.\n\n## Acceptance Rate\n\nThe search results mention that acceptance rates can be computed, but they don't provide the specific acceptance rate for CoRL 2024 or 2025. Acceptance rates are calculated as the number of accepted papers divided by the total number of submissions (for example, if there are 100 total submissions and 27 were accepted, the accept rate = 27%).\n\n## Scoring Rubric\n\nUnfortunately, the search results don't contain specific details about a detailed scoring rubric for CoRL reviewers. The results reference general review criteria but not a comprehensive numerical scoring system or rubric.\n\nFor the most current and detailed reviewer guidelines and scoring rubrics, I recommend checking the official CoRL website or OpenReview page directly, as these documents may not be fully indexed in search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f290d644-682c-40ce-bbe2-cd72e060667b","uuid":"7740baad-c4f6-49ee-a131-f36d82fd7c3a","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:44:14.000Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 2024 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric acceptance rate","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_017RDdXTa3wXdk7cfENhriSG","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2025 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2025-paper-list/"},{"title":"CORL 2025 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2025-statistics/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2024-paper-list/"},{"ti