{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Er6LpobEjCeRnv4iFGiscE","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL OpenReview review form overall score rating scale 1-10\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Default Review Form | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"Why are the \\\"rating\\\" and \\\"confidence\\\" fields in my PC Console wrong? | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/getting-started/frequently-asked-questions/why-are-the-rating-and-confidence-fields-in-my-pc-console-wrong\"},{\"title\":\"Paper Ranking Methodology\",\"url\":\"https://openreview-copilot.eamag.me/ranking\"},{\"title\":\"Reference-Free Rating of LLM Responses via Latent Information | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=WoYvrulVOp\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR2020 Open Review Explorer\",\"url\":\"https://horace.io/OpenReviewExplorer/\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397780200_Insights_from_the_ICLR_Peer_Review_and_Rebuttal_Process\"},{\"title\":\"OpenReviewer: A Specialized Large Language Model for Generating Critical Scientific Paper Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.11948v3\"},{\"title\":\"Integrating Rankings into Quantized Scores in Peer Review | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=Kb1lb0vSLa\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the OpenReview rating scale used for review forms. The OpenReview default review form uses a 1-10 rating scale with the following descriptions: 10 (Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper), 9 (Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept), 8 (Top 50% of accepted papers, clear accept), 7 (Good paper, accept), 6 (Marginally above acceptance threshold), 5 (Marginally below acceptance threshold), 4 (Ok but not good enough - rejection), 3 (Clear rejection), 2 (Strong rejection), and 1 (Trivial or wrong).\n\nThis is the standard OpenReview rating scale that is used for conference review forms, including CoRL submissions. The scale is designed to provide detailed guidance for reviewers on what each numerical score should represent in terms of paper quality and acceptance decisions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f290d644-682c-40ce-bbe2-cd72e060667b","uuid":"2180df1b-ea5e-410b-9329-83d17b2b4a63","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:44:36.217Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL OpenReview review form overall score rating scale 1-10","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01KXyqRHUAJiHa2MU46QwWtr","content":[{"title":"Default Review Form | OpenReview","url":"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"Why are the \"rating\" and \"confidence\" fields in my PC Console wrong? | OpenReview","url":"https://docs.openreview.net/getting-started/frequently-asked-questions/why-are-the-rating-and-confidence-fields-in-my-pc-console-wrong"},{"title":"Paper Ranking Methodology","url":"https://openreview-copilot.eamag.me/ranking"},{"title":"Reference-Free Rating of LLM Responses via Latent Information | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=WoYvrulVOp"},{"title":"ICLR2020 Open Review Explorer","url":"https://horace.io/OpenReviewExplorer/"},{"title":"(PDF) Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/397780200_Insights_from_the_ICLR_Peer_Review_and_Rebuttal_Process"},{"title":"OpenReviewer: A Specialized Large Language Model for Generating Critical Scientific Paper Reviews","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2412.11948v3"},{"title":"Integrating Rankings into Quantized Scores in Peer Review | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/forum?id=Kb1lb0vSLa"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about the OpenReview rating scale used for review forms. The OpenReview default review form uses a 1-10 rating scale with the following descriptions: 10 (Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper), 9 (Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept), 8 (Top 50% of accepted papers, clear accept), 7 (Good paper, accept), 6 (Marginally above acceptance threshold), 5 (Marginally below acceptance threshold), 4 (Ok but not good enough - rejection), 3 (Clear rejection), 2 (Strong rejection), and 1 (Trivial or wrong).\n\nThis is the standard OpenReview rating scale that is used for conference review forms, including CoRL submissions. The scale is designed to provide detailed guidance for reviewers on what each numerical score should represent in terms of paper quality and acceptance decisions."],"durationSeconds":6.793554175999998}}
