{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BdDybA37nHMvdXQXawhE2b","type":"tool_result","content":"# CoRL Acceptance Rates by Year\n\nBased on the Paper Copilot statistics page, here are the submission and acceptance data:\n\n**CoRL 2025**\n- Total Submissions: 263\n- Accepted Papers: 221 (84.03%)\n- Note: \"221 (84.03%)\" represents posters, suggesting this may reflect a different acceptance structure than prior years\n\n**CoRL 2024**\n- Total Submissions: 671\n- Accepted Papers: 264 (39.34%)\n- Location: Munich, Germany\n\n**CoRL 2023**\n- Total Submissions: 498\n- Accepted Papers: 199 (39.96%)\n- Location: Atlanta, USA\n\n**CoRL 2022**\n- Total Submissions: 504\n- Accepted Papers: 197 (39.09%)\n\n**CoRL 2021**\n- Total Submissions: 408\n- Accepted Papers: 153 (37.50%)\n\nThe data shows that CoRL 2024 and 2025 have notably different acceptance patterns, with 2025 showing significantly higher acceptance rates. However, the 2025 data structure differs from previous years, so direct comparisons may not be straightforward."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f290d644-682c-40ce-bbe2-cd72e060667b","uuid":"87c1cc2c-5f6a-4b27-a84b-e6012ab4fa60","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:44:44.396Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":143480,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CoRL Acceptance Rates by Year\n\nBased on the Paper Copilot statistics page, here are the submission and acceptance data:\n\n**CoRL 2025**\n- Total Submissions: 263\n- Accepted Papers: 221 (84.03%)\n- Note: \"221 (84.03%)\" represents posters, suggesting this may reflect a different acceptance structure than prior years\n\n**CoRL 2024**\n- Total Submissions: 671\n- Accepted Papers: 264 (39.34%)\n- Location: Munich, Germany\n\n**CoRL 2023**\n- Total Submissions: 498\n- Accepted Papers: 199 (39.96%)\n- Location: Atlanta, USA\n\n**CoRL 2022**\n- Total Submissions: 504\n- Accepted Papers: 197 (39.09%)\n\n**CoRL 2021**\n- Total Submissions: 408\n- Accepted Papers: 153 (37.50%)\n\nThe data shows that CoRL 2024 and 2025 have notably different acceptance patterns, with 2025 showing significantly higher acceptance rates. However, the 2025 data structure differs from previous years, so direct comparisons may not be straightforward.","durationMs":3785,"url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/"}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01BxSgd6NdHBCV9Zn3NxgQ8H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough context. Let me compile the CoRL review standards:\n\n- CoRL acceptance rate is ~39% historically (2022-2024)\n- OpenReview 1-10 scale\n- 6 evaluation dimensions from CoRL 2023: Originality, Quality, Clarity, Significance, Relevance, Limitations\n- Robot learning relevance is critical\n\nNow I need to dispatch 2 reviewers:\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nThen conduct a 4-step roundtable. Let me dispatch both reviewers in parallel as agents.\n\n\nI'll structure this by sending both reviewers out simultaneously, then once I have their independent assessments, I'll move through the roundtable discussion where they share findings, converge on key points, and synthesize a final recommendation before submitting the review report.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":452,"cache_read_input_tokens":67275,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":452},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f290d644-682c-40ce-bbe2-cd72e060667b","uuid":"8078e010-d7a7-4ae4-b4fa-d7c80dd7932c"}
