{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XNPjSqbMQA77jvLYdUV7o3","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515/projects/meta_brain_lora_routing/ROADMAP.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# meta_brain_lora_routing — Research Dashboard\\\\n\\\\n> 最后更新: 2026-05-15 15:47 UTC | 更新原因: Post-MVP kickoff: 引用 paper_framing.md + experiment_plan.yaml, Dream 已启动\\\\n\\\\n## 核心方向\\\\nPerturbation-Adaptive LoRA Routing：从冻结 π₀ 内部激活诊断扰动类型，路由到专用 LoRA expert 做针对性修正。详见 `paper_framing.md`。\\\\n\\\\n## 目标会议\\\\nCoRL 2026 — Abstract DDL: 2026-05-26 (11天)，Paper DDL: 2026-05-29 (14天)\\\\n\\\\n## Core Claims (from paper_framing.md)\\\\n1. **Perturbation Diagnosability** — 单层单步即可完美分类扰动类型 (Phase 0 验证通过)\\\\n2. **Targeted > Uniform Correction** — 扰动专用 LoRA > 通用 LoRA (Phase 1 待验证)\\\\n3. **Parameter-Efficient Robustness** — 6M params vs VLA-GSE 114M (Phase 1+2 待验证)\\\\n\\\\n## 当前进展\\\\n- 阶段：**Research** (MVP 通过 2026-05-15)\\\\n- Phase 0 ✅ GO: 3-class F1=0.993, K=1 F1=0.898, layer6 K=1=1.0\\\\n- Phase 1: 准备中 — 等待 Dream 模拟回调 (`dream_20260515T154653`) 后批准 P0 实验\\\\n- 实验计划: 12 个实验 (P0: 5, P1: 3, P2: 4)，详见 `experiment_plan.yaml`\\\\n- 覆盖率: 用 `compute_coverage_matrix()` 派生，不手画\\\\n\\\\n## 近期任务\\\\n- [x] Phase 0 GO 判定 (D004)\\\\n- [x] complete_mvp() 进入 research 阶段\\\\n- [x] 写 paper_framing.md\\\\n- [x] 写 experiment_plan.yaml\\\\n- [x] 启动 dream_simulate(review_mode=\\\\\\\"full\\\\\\\")\\\\n- [ ] 等 Dream 回调 → 审视 framing/plan 是否需要调整\\\\n- [ ] 批准 P0 实验 (plan_002: LoRA training, plan_003: assembly)\\\\n- [ ] Phase 1 LoRA training 代码准备 + 数据准备\\\\n- [ ] Phase 1 训练启动（4 GPU 并行: LoRA-V/S/P + Universal）\\\\n\\\\n## Phase 0 残留项（并行补完，不阻塞 Phase 1）\\\\n- [ ] objects_layout + robot_initial_states per_step 数据重收集 + 完整 3-class few-shot\\\\n- [ ] sensor_noise 重收集（等 LIBERO-Plus assets 下载）\\\\n- [ ] eval_classifier.py 修正（只报告 CV 数字）\\\\n\\\\n## GPU 预算\\\\n- 当前分配：4× RTX PRO 6000 96GB @ westd-34142\\\\n- 已用：~25 GPU-hrs（Phase 0）\\\\n- 计划：P0=95h, P1=25h, P2=65h，总计 185h（190h 预算内）\\\\n\\\\n## 架构决策 (from Phase 0)\\\\n- Router: PaliGemma layer 6 单层, mean pooling, 2-layer MLP\\\\n- LoRA: 作用于 PaliGemma 层（Expert 不编码扰动差异）\\\\n- 路由延迟: 单次前向传播即可决策\\\\n\\\\n## 关键决策日志\\\\n\\\\n| ID | 日期 | 摘要 | 关联实验 |\\\\n|----|------|------|----------|\\\\n| D006 | 2026-05-15 | PAR Router 改用 first-token pooling（F1 1.000 vs mean | phase0_activation_collection |\\\\n| D005 | 2026-05-15 | 进入 Research 阶段 — 完成 paper_framing.md + experiment_ | phase0_activation_collection |\\\\n| D004 | 2026-05-15 | Phase 0 GO — 核心假设验证通过，进入 Phase 1 LoRA expert 训练 | phase0_activation_collection |\\\\n| D003 | 2026-05-15 | Phase 0 架构修正：层索引改为 Gemma 2B 的 18 层范围 + 排除 Language | — |\\\\n| D002 | 2026-05-15 | 采纳 Reviewer 4 条建议增强 Phase 0：+binary sanity check,  | — |\\\\n| D001 | 2026-05-15 | MVP 定义为 Phase 0 early-kill gate：验证 π₀ 内部激活能否分类 3 类 | — |\\\\n\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2348, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WDJwwiziRzCzZJENTqR7y4","session_id":"f290d644-682c-40ce-bbe2-cd72e060667b","uuid":"f9e3e4a1-c303-4dbc-a45b-f9f87fe8a460","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:45:56.820Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0195xkF4veVokbMCRHk4MXtL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — meta_brain_lora_routing\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: CoRL 2026 (Austin, Nov 9-12)\n5\t- Abstract DDL: 2026-05-26\n6\t- Paper DDL: 2026-05-29\n7\t\n8\t## Core Insight\n9\t\n10\tVLA internal representations already encode rich perturbation-type-specific information (Phase 0: single-layer F1=1.0 at K=1), yet existing robustness methods either ignore this diagnostic signal entirely (VLA-GSE, RobustVLA) or only use it for detection without correction (SAFE). Meta-Brain closes the loop: diagnose perturbation type from frozen activations, then route to a type-specialized LoRA expert for targeted correction — achieving the \"right fix for the right failure\" at 20x fewer parameters than perturbation-agnostic capacity routing.\n11\t\n12\t## Core Claims (3)\n13\t\n14\t1. **Perturbation Diagnosability** — Frozen VLA (pi0) internal activations at a single layer (PaliGemma layer 6) encode perturbation type with near-perfect accuracy (3-class macro-F1 >= 0.99), enabling real-time, zero-overhead perturbation diagnosis from a single forward pass.\n15\t\n16\t2. **Targeted Correction > Uniform Correction** — Perturbation-type-specific LoRA experts (Visual/Spatial/Physical), routed by the diagnosed type, outperform a universal LoRA baseline of equivalent total parameter budget on LIBERO-Plus, demonstrating that routing by perturbation type is a more efficient use of adaptation capacity than uniform correction.\n17\t\n18\t3. **Parameter-Efficient Robustness** — Meta-Brain (~6M trainable params: 3x rank-16 LoRA + PAR router) achieves competitive robustness gain-over-frozen-baseline compared to VLA-GSE (114M params), establishing perturbation-diagnostic routing as a parameter-efficient alternative to capacity-based expert routing.\n19\t\n20\t## Story Spine\n21\t\n22\t- **Problem**: VLAs achieve >90% on standard LIBERO but collapse under perturbation (pi0: 53.6% on LIBERO-Plus). Different perturbation types disrupt different processing stages — visual perturbations corrupt early representations, spatial perturbations invalidate action trajectories, physical perturbations break force assumptions. Yet all existing robustness methods apply either single-modality correction or perturbation-agnostic uniform adaptation.\n23\t\n24\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: VLA-GSE (114M params, 81.2% on LIBERO-Plus) demonstrates routing helps, but routes by per-token capacity needs — the same gating configuration handles camera (64.4%) and layout (82.6%) without perturbation awareness. FTM achieves 90% on visual perturbations with 4K params but cannot handle spatial/physical. RobustVLA adds +12.6% via uniform adversarial training. No method combines perturbation diagnosis with type-specific correction.\n25\t\n26\t- **Our framing**: We propose perturbation-diagnostic routing as a new design dimension for VLA robustness, orthogonal to capacity-based routing (VLA-GSE), rank-based adaptation (LoRA-SP), and task-based routing (MoIRA/CORAL). We show that VLA internals already \"know\" what went wrong — they just lack the mechanism to apply the right fix. Meta-Brain adds that mechanism with minimal parameters.\n27\t\n28\t- **Headline result template**: \"On LIBERO-Plus, Meta-Brain achieves X% with 6M trainable parameters, improving Y% over frozen pi0 baseline and Z% over a parameter-matched universal LoRA, while VLA-GSE requires 114M parameters to achieve 81.2%.\"\n29\t\n30\t## Contribution Structure\n31\t\n32\t1. **Empirical finding**: VLA internal representations encode perturbation type at single-layer, single-step granularity — enabling real-time diagnosis without external modules or multi-step observation buffers\n33\t2. **Architecture**: Meta-Brain — a modular, parameter-efficient framework (PAR router + LoRA bank + optional Correction Memory) that routes corrective LoRA experts by diagnosed perturbation type\n34\t3. **Design dimension analysis**: Systematic comparison of perturbation-diagnostic routing vs. capacity-based routing vs. universal adaptation, establishing perturbation-awareness as an orthogonal and composable design axis\n35\t\n36\t## Venue Fit (CoRL 2026)\n37\t\n38\t**Strengths**:\n39\t- Pi0 backbone + LIBERO-Plus eval is core CoRL territory\n40\t- Architecture operates on representations (sim evaluation methodologically sufficient)\n41\t- Parameter efficiency matters for real-robot deployment (6M vs 114M)\n42\t- Single forward pass routing = no latency overhead for real-time control\n43\t\n44\t**Risks**:\n45\t- Sim-only evaluation (mitigated: LIBERO-Plus is CVPR 2026 standard, sim-only is accepted pattern at CoRL for architecture contributions)\n46\t- Single backbone (pi0) — need gain-over-baseline framing to enable contextualized comparison with VLA-GSE (Qwen3-VL-4B)\n47\t- Absolute performance may trail SRPO (82.1%) / CorridorVLA (83.21%) which use full training — frame as parameter-efficient approach, not absolute SOTA chase\n48\t\n49\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n50\t\n51\t### C1: \"Phase 0 classification is too easy — trivially solvable routing\"\n52\t**Risk**: High Phase 0 accuracy (F1=0.993) may suggest the task is trivial and routing adds no value.\n53\t**Response**: Easy diagnosis ≠ easy correction. The value of routing is in Phase 1 (specialized vs universal LoRA), not Phase 0. Easy routing is actually desirable — it means the router adds zero overhead concern. Ablation exp-005 directly tests whether routing matters.\n54\t\n55\t### C2: \"Sim-only evaluation, no real robot\"\n56\t**Risk**: CoRL values real-world experiments.\n57\t**Response**: LIBERO-Plus is the standard robustness benchmark (CVPR 2026). Meta-Brain operates on representations, not hardware-specific signals. Sim-only is the established evaluation pattern for VLA architecture contributions at CoRL (SAFE, VLA-GSE, RobustVLA all sim-only on LIBERO variants).\n58\t\n59\t### C3: \"Single backbone (pi0), limited generalizability\"\n60\t**Risk**: Results may be specific to pi0's PaliGemma architecture.\n61\t**Response**: (a) Phase 0 finding (perturbation classifiability) is grounded in mechanistic evidence across multiple VLAs (SAFE on OpenVLA, probing on OpenVLA, feature steering on pi0.5 + OpenVLA). (b) Tier 3 cross-backbone experiment on SmolVLA/OpenVLA if time permits. (c) Gain-over-baseline metric enables fair comparison across backbones.\n62\t\n63\t### C4: \"Parameter budget comparison unfair — different backbone from VLA-GSE\"\n64\t**Risk**: Comparing 6M (on pi0) vs 114M (on Qwen3-VL-4B) is apples-to-oranges.\n65\t**Response**: Compare gain-over-respective-LoRA-baseline: VLA-GSE gains +12.0% over LoRA (69.2% → 81.2%); Meta-Brain should gain X% over universal LoRA on pi0. Parameter efficiency = gain per trainable parameter. Also report absolute numbers with caveat.\n66\t\n67\t### C5: \"3-class taxonomy may be too coarse\"\n68\t**Risk**: Lumping camera+light+background+noise into \"Visual\" may lose useful distinctions.\n69\t**Response**: Phase 0 6-class analysis shows intra-Visual perturbations are more similar to each other than to Spatial/Physical. 3-class matches the mechanistic distinction in VLA processing (early/mid/late layers). Ablation: 6-class routing vs 3-class routing comparison.\n70\t\n71\t### C6: \"Correction Memory adds complexity for marginal gain\"\n72\t**Risk**: CM may seem over-engineered for routing-weight modulation.\n73\t**Response**: CM is presented as an optional module. Ablation (with/without CM) quantifies its contribution. CM adds only 1 learned parameter (alpha) + CPU-bound FAISS.\n74\t\n75\t## Baselines & Comparisons\n76\t\n77\t| Method | Type | Params | Expected Comparison |\n78\t|--------|------|--------|-------------------|\n79\t| Frozen pi0 | Lower bound | 0 | Our improvement over this = headline number |\n80\t| Universal LoRA (rank 16) | Ablation | ~2M | Same total capacity, no routing — tests Claim 2 |\n81\t| Meta-Brain (PAR + ALB) | Ours | ~6M | Full system |\n82\t| Meta-Brain + CM | Ours (full) | ~6M + 1 | With Correction Memory |\n83\t| Oracle routing | Upper bound | ~6M | Perfect routing — gap to Meta-Brain = routing quality |\n84\t| FTM/FLA | Visual-only | 4K-4.7M | Strong on visual, cannot do spatial/physical |\n85\t| VLA-GSE | Capacity routing | 114M | Different backbone (Qwen3-VL-4B), compare gain-over-LoRA |\n86\t| RobustVLA | Adversarial training | Full model | Uniform approach, compare robustness gain |\n87\t\n88\t## Key Figures (Planned)\n89\t\n90\t1. **Architecture diagram**: Frozen pi0 → PAR (layer 6) → soft routing → LoRA-V/S/P bank → corrected output\n91\t2. **Phase 0 evidence**: t-SNE of layer 6 activations colored by perturbation type + confusion matrix\n92\t3. **Main result table**: LIBERO-Plus per-perturbation breakdown (7 categories × methods)\n93\t4. **Ablation ladder**: Bar chart — Frozen → Universal LoRA → Meta-Brain → Oracle\n94\t5. **Parameter efficiency**: Scatter plot — gain-over-baseline vs trainable parameters (Meta-Brain vs VLA-GSE vs FTM vs RobustVLA)\n95\t6. **Routing analysis**: Heatmap of PAR soft routing weights per perturbation type (should be near-diagonal)\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KgS46ueuGs5A8Jd8wKpTUy","session_id":"f290d644-682c-40ce-bbe2-cd72e060667b","uuid":"7908a912-9d8a-4e20-b5c6-d73abda41ca8","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:45:56.909Z"}
