{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HkMWrQyRdVJmrWP8ffKdbg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Meta-Brain Experiment Plan\n2\t# Generated: 2026-05-15\n3\t# Claims reference: paper_framing.md\n4\t\n5\texperiments:\n6\t  # ═══════════════ Claim 1: Perturbation Diagnosability ═══════════════\n7\t\n8\t  - id: plan_001\n9\t    claim: 1\n10\t    title: \"Phase 0 — Perturbation classification from frozen activations\"\n11\t    description: >\n12\t      Train 2-layer MLP on frozen pi0 PaliGemma activations for 3-class perturbation\n13\t      classification (Visual/Spatial/Physical). Sweep layers, pooling strategies, learning rates.\n14\t      Includes binary sanity check, 6-class comparison, few-shot K=1/3/5/10 analysis.\n15\t    priority: P0\n16\t    status: done\n17\t    registry_id: phase0_activation_collection\n18\t    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n19\t    deps: []\n20\t    key_results: \"3-class F1=0.993, binary AUC=1.0, K=1 F1=0.898, layer6 K=1=1.0\"\n21\t\n22\t  # ═══════════════ Claim 2: Targeted > Uniform Correction ═══════════════\n23\t\n24\t  - id: plan_002\n25\t    claim: 2\n26\t    title: \"LoRA expert training — 3 perturbation-specific + 1 universal baseline\"\n27\t    description: >\n28\t      Train 4 LoRA adapters on frozen pi0 PaliGemma attention layers (rank 16, Q/K/V/O projections):\n29\t      (a) LoRA-V: trained on Visual perturbation rollouts (camera+light+background+noise)\n30\t      (b) LoRA-S: trained on Spatial perturbation rollouts (layout)\n31\t      (c) LoRA-P: trained on Physical perturbation rollouts (robot)\n32\t      (d) Universal LoRA: trained on mixed all-perturbation rollouts\n33\t      Each on 1 GPU in parallel (4 GPUs total).\n34\t\n35\t      Training data strategy (two-pronged):\n36\t      (a) Visual perturbations (LoRA-V): Use LIBERO standard expert demonstrations with ONLINE\n37\t          visual augmentation during training (camera jitter, brightness/contrast shifts,\n38\t          background texture swap, Gaussian noise). Action labels are unchanged because visual\n39\t          perturbations don't alter the physical task. This is analogous to FTM's training setup.\n40\t      (b) Spatial/Physical perturbations (LoRA-S, LoRA-P): Use LIBERO's scripted oracle policies\n41\t          to collect new expert demonstrations in LIBERO-Plus perturbed environments (layout\n42\t          randomization, robot initial state randomization). ~200 successful demos per category.\n43\t          Fallback: if oracle policy unavailable, use DAgger-style collection with frozen pi0\n44\t          (collect partial successes + human corrections).\n45\t      (c) Universal LoRA: Mix of all above data sources.\n46\t      Training objective: SFT (behavior cloning) — minimize flow-matching action prediction\n47\t      loss on (perturbed_observation, correct_action) pairs. Match pi0's action head format.\n48\t      Convergence criterion: validation action MSE plateaus for 3 consecutive eval checkpoints.\n49\t      LoRA config: rank 16 on Q/K/V/O of ALL PaliGemma attention layers (18 layers).\n50\t      All 3 experts use identical layer coverage initially (per Reviewer feedback — Phase 0\n51\t      shows <2.5pp spread across layers, no evidence for layer-specific assignment).\n52\t      Layer placement ablation deferred to plan_012.\n53\t\n54\t      Evaluate each expert on its own perturbation type AND cross-type (mismatched expert).\n55\t    priority: P0\n56\t    gpu_budget_hours: 55\n57\t    deps: []\n58\t    metrics:\n59\t      - per_expert_success_rate_on_own_type\n60\t      - per_expert_success_rate_cross_type\n61\t      - universal_lora_success_rate_all_types\n62\t\n63\t  - id: plan_003\n64\t    claim: 2\n65\t    title: \"Meta-Brain assembly — PAR router + LoRA bank end-to-end\"\n66\t    description: >\n67\t      Assemble PAR router (PaliGemma layer 6, 2-layer MLP) + 3 LoRA experts with\n68\t      soft routing: h_corrected = h_frozen + sum_k p(type_k) * LoRA_k(h_frozen).\n69\t      End-to-end routing fine-tuning with frozen LoRA parameters (only tune PAR routing weights).\n70\t      Evaluate on full LIBERO-Plus benchmark (all 7 perturbation types × all task suites).\n71\t    priority: P0\n72\t    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n73\t    deps: [plan_002]\n74\t    metrics:\n75\t      - libero_plus_overall_success_rate\n76\t      - per_perturbation_success_rate_breakdown\n77\t      - routing_weight_distribution_per_type\n78\t\n79\t  - id: plan_004\n80\t    claim: 2\n81\t    title: \"Oracle routing ablation — upper bound for routing quality\"\n82\t    description: >\n83\t      Replace PAR router with ground-truth perturbation type labels (oracle routing).\n84\t      Measures the gap between learned routing and perfect routing.\n85\t      If gap is small, PAR is sufficient; if large, router needs improvement.\n86\t    priority: P1\n87\t    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n88\t    deps: [plan_002]\n89\t    metrics:\n90\t      - oracle_vs_par_success_rate_gap\n91\t\n92\t  - id: plan_005\n93\t    claim: 2\n94\t    title: \"Ablation ladder — Frozen → Universal LoRA → Random → Meta-Brain → Oracle\"\n95\t    description: >\n96\t      Systematic comparison on LIBERO-Plus with 5 seeds:\n97\t      (a) Frozen pi0 baseline (no adaptation)\n98\t      (b) Universal LoRA (rank 16, ~2M params)\n99\t      (c) Random routing (randomly assign one of 3 LoRA experts per episode — controls\n100\t          for ensemble effect. If random ≈ Meta-Brain, Claim 2 is falsified)\n101\t      (d) Meta-Brain (PAR + 3 LoRA experts, ~6M params)\n102\t      (e) Oracle routing (ground-truth type → LoRA expert)\n103\t      Report overall success rate + per-perturbation breakdown.\n104\t      This is the core evidence for Claim 2. The critical comparison is (c) vs (d):\n105\t      Meta-Brain must significantly outperform random routing to prove routing matters.\n106\t    priority: P0\n107\t    gpu_budget_hours: 25\n108\t    deps: [plan_003, plan_004]\n109\t    metrics:\n110\t      - ablation_ladder_table\n111\t      - gain_over_frozen_per_method\n112\t      - gain_over_universal_lora\n113\t      - meta_brain_vs_random_routing_gap\n114\t\n115\t  # ═══════════════ Claim 3: Parameter-Efficient Robustness ═══════════════\n116\t\n117\t  - id: plan_006\n118\t    claim: 3\n119\t    title: \"FTM/FLA reproduction — visual-only baseline comparison\"\n120\t    description: >\n121\t      Reproduce FTM on pi0 for visual perturbation types (camera, light, background, noise).\n122\t      Compare Meta-Brain LoRA-V vs FTM on visual perturbations.\n123\t      Meta-Brain must show value beyond FTM by additionally handling spatial/physical.\n124\t    priority: P1\n125\t    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n126\t    deps: []\n127\t    metrics:\n128\t      - ftm_vs_lora_v_on_visual_perturbations\n129\t      - meta_brain_advantage_on_non_visual\n130\t\n131\t  - id: plan_007\n132\t    claim: 3\n133\t    title: \"Parameter efficiency analysis — gain-over-baseline vs trainable params\"\n134\t    description: >\n135\t      Compute gain-over-frozen-baseline per method and normalize by trainable parameters.\n136\t      Plot scatter: x=trainable params (log scale), y=gain-over-baseline.\n137\t      Include: Meta-Brain (12M), Universal LoRA (3.7M), FTM (4K-4.7M), VLA-GSE (114M, from paper).\n138\t      This is the visual evidence for Claim 3.\n139\t    priority: P0\n140\t    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n141\t    deps: [plan_005, plan_006]\n142\t    metrics:\n143\t      - parameter_efficiency_scatter_plot\n144\t      - gain_per_million_params\n145\t\n146\t  # ═══════════════ Tier 2 Ablations ═══════════════\n147\t\n148\t  - id: plan_008\n149\t    claim: 2\n150\t    title: \"Correction Memory ablation — with/without CM\"\n151\t    description: >\n152\t      Compare Meta-Brain with and without Correction Memory module.\n153\t      CM adds routing-weight modulation from retrieved exemplars.\n154\t      Quantify marginal gain of CM on overall and per-perturbation success.\n155\t    priority: P1\n156\t    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n157\t    deps: [plan_003]\n158\t    metrics:\n159\t      - cm_ablation_delta\n160\t      - cm_benefit_per_perturbation_type\n161\t\n162\t  - id: plan_009\n163\t    claim: 1\n164\t    title: \"Router architecture comparison — MLP vs linear vs attention\"\n165\t    description: >\n166\t      Compare PAR variants: (a) 2-layer MLP (default), (b) linear classifier,\n167\t      (c) attention-based router. All on PaliGemma layer 6.\n168\t      Measures whether routing accuracy changes translate to downstream task success.\n169\t    priority: P2\n170\t    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n171\t    deps: [plan_002]\n172\t    metrics:\n173\t      - router_accuracy_comparison\n174\t      - downstream_success_by_router_type\n175\t\n176\t  - id: plan_010\n177\t    claim: 2\n178\t    title: \"6-class vs 3-class routing comparison\"\n179\t    description: >\n180\t      Compare 6-class fine-grained routing (camera/light/background/noise/layout/robot)\n181\t      with 6 LoRA experts vs 3-class coarse routing (Visual/Spatial/Physical) with 3 experts.\n182\t      Tests whether finer-grained routing justifies additional parameters.\n183\t    priority: P2\n184\t    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n185\t    deps: [plan_002]\n186\t    metrics:\n187\t      - 6class_vs_3class_overall_success\n188\t      - marginal_gain_per_additional_expert\n189\t\n190\t  # ═══════════════ Tier 3 Extensions ═══════════════\n191\t\n192\t  - id: plan_011\n193\t    claim: 3\n194\t    title: \"Cross-backbone validation — SmolVLA or OpenVLA\"\n195\t    description: >\n196\t      Replicate Phase 0 + Phase 1 core pipeline on a second VLA backbone\n197\t      (SmolVLA or OpenVLA) to test generalizability of the perturbation-diagnostic\n198\t      routing principle across architectures.\n199\t    priority: P2\n200\t    gpu_budget_hours: 30\n201\t    deps: [plan_005]\n202\t    metrics:\n203\t      - cross_backbone_phase0_f1\n204\t      - cross_backbone_gain_over_baseline\n205\t\n206\t  - id: plan_012\n207\t    claim: 2\n208\t    title: \"LoRA layer placement ablation\"\n209\t    description: >\n210\t      Vary which PaliGemma layers receive LoRA experts:\n211\t      (a) early layers only (2-6), (b) mid layers (6-12), (c) late layers (12-16),\n212\t      (d) all layers. Test hypothesis that Visual LoRA benefits from early layers,\n213\t      Spatial from mid, Physical from late.\n214\t    priority: P2\n215\t    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n216\t    deps: [plan_002]\n217\t    metrics:\n218\t      - optimal_layer_placement_per_expert_type\n219\t\n220\t# ═══════════════ Budget Summary ═══════════════\n221\t# P0 total: 100 GPU-hrs (plan_001: 5, plan_002: 55, plan_003: 15, plan_005: 25, plan_007: 0)\n222\t# P1 total: 25 GPU-hrs (plan_004: 5, plan_006: 10, plan_008: 10)\n223\t# P2 total: 65 GPU-hrs (plan_009: 5, plan_010: 15, plan_011: 30, plan_012: 15)\n224\t# Grand total: 190 GPU-hrs (within budget, adjusted for RTX PRO 6000)\n225\t# Available: 4x RTX PRO 6000 96GB @ westd-34142\n226\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WDJwwiziRzCzZJENTqR7y4","session_id":"f290d644-682c-40ce-bbe2-cd72e060667b","uuid":"580164c6-96d4-4d59-8dd6-e162fd482d0c","timestamp":"2026-05-15T16:46:19.366Z"}
